//    any British word with no frequency of its own borrows the frequency of
//    its predictable American counterpart via general spelling-pattern rules
//    (our→or, ise→ize, re→er, ogue→og, lled→led, ence→ense, ould→old, ae/oe→e).
//    That's precomputed once when this file is built, not run in the browser.)
